      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mitosis is a process where a single cell divides into two identical daughter cells. This is crucial for growth, development, and tissue repair in our bodies. The process involves several stages: prophase, metaphase, anaphase, and telophase. During prophase, the chromosomes condense and become visible. In metaphase, they align in the middle of the cell. Anaphase sees the chromosomes being pulled apart to opposite ends. Finally, telophase and cytokinesis complete the division, resulting in two identical cells. Understanding mitosis helps us appreciate how our bodies grow and heal. Learning this can be really helpful for your studies in biology.",
      "source": "target",
